cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "agda-lattices: lattice theory in Agda"
abstract: >-
  A formalization of lattice theory in Agda, on top of the Agda Universal
  Algebra Library: lattice terms and Whitman's solution of the word problem
  for free lattices, the free lattice and its universal property, canonical
  forms and the terms of least rank, Whitman's condition and
  semidistributivity, substitutions, free generating sets, the generators
  and automorphisms of a free lattice, embeddings and complexity, Whitman's
  countable family, and membership in a finitely generated sublattice,
  decided; the prime elements of a lattice generated by a set; free
  generation and breadth in lattices satisfying Whitman's condition; bounded
  homomorphisms, projective lattices and Kostinsky's theorem; Nation's
  theorem for finite lattices, with its easy direction and Nation's argument
  that a finite lattice with both semidistributive laws and Whitman's
  condition is bounded; quotients, intervals, sublattices, direct limits,
  modular and distributive lattices, central elements and direct
  decompositions, finite products, and lattices given by their operation
  tables.  Each result of Chapter I of Freese, Ježek and Nation's Free
  Lattices that the library proves in full, and Lemma 9.13, is also one
  statement, named by its number in the book or its standard theorem name.
  Every module is checked under --without-K --exact-split --safe.
